deko3d: resolves into part of a texture; target heights bounded by the EDRAM.

- MGR resolves its two shadow cascades, each drawn at 1024x1024, into one 1024x2048 texture: the
  second one 4 MB past the first, the start of the lower half. Textures being images keyed by
  address, the second made a texture nothing samples and the lower half stayed empty.
  ResueltaQueContiene finds the texture whose memory holds a resolve's address at the start of a
  row of tiles, and the resolve is written there, that many rows down.
- A target's height came from its pitch only (1280 rows for a pitch of 1280). It is now also
  bounded by what fits between its base and the end of the EDRAM: MGR's scene targets at base
  0x530 are 1280x720, the size of their textures, so a whole resolve can swap images instead of
  copying (nfsmw_nativo_resolver_sin_copia).

